---

LLMD is ZML's LLM server that runs many models on any platform at full speed.
You can even try it on your laptop.

# [Before you run]($heading.id('what-you-need'))

```=html
<div class="llmd-first-run-prerequisites">
  <p>Use an Apple Silicon Mac with macOS Tahoe or later, Homebrew, and access to Hugging Face.</p>
  <p>On M1 and M2, use LLMD 20261112.0 or later.</p>
</div>
```

For another model or accelerator, see [Start LLMD on any platform]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/start')).


# [Run the server]($heading.id('run-local-server'))

```=html
<div class="llmd-first-run-pair">
  <section>
    <h3>Install once</h3>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy first-run install command">brew install zml/zml/llmd</code></pre>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h3>Start LLMD</h3>
    <p>LLMD downloads the model at startup. Leave this terminal running.</p>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy first-run launch command">llmd --model=hf://LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B \
  --listen=127.0.0.1:8000</code></pre>
  </section>
</div>
```

# [Send a chat request]($heading.id('first-chat-request'))

After the model loads, send this request from a second terminal.

```=html
<div class="llmd-first-run-pair">
  <section>
    <h3>Request</h3>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy first-run chat request">curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "model": "LFM3-1.7B",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Reply with one short greeting."}]
  }'</code></pre>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h3>Example response</h3>
    <pre><code class="json">{
  "choices": [
    {"message": {"content": "Hello!"}}
  ]
}</code></pre>
    <p>Read the reply in <code>choices[0].message.content</code>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
```

[Troubleshoot startup]($link.page('llmd/howto/monitoring-and-troubleshooting').ref('diagnose-common-failures'))
